<title>FRANCE: Nouvelles Frontieres confirms AOM airline talks.</title>
<headline>Nouvelles Frontieres confirms AOM airline talks.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>A spokeswoman for travel group Nouvelles Frontieres confirmed remarks by chairman Jacques Maillot in a newspaper that he was in talks to acquire French airline AOM.</p>
<p>Maillot, who withdrew from bidding for ailing Air Liberte on Tuesday afternoon, had planned to merge his Corsair, Air Liberte and AOM to create a second strong French private group alongside Air France.</p>
<p>Maillot himself was not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>British Airways was sole bidder for Air Liberte.</p>
</text>
